; clojure.core/locking is defined, but any use fails to compile: its expansion calls
; monitor-enter, which jank does not define ("The symbol clojure.core/monitor-enter could not be
; resolved"). Clojure runs the body holding the object's monitor.
(def lock (atom 0))
(println "expected 2:" (locking lock (+ 1 1)))
